  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116402",
      "title": "Setting Up & Navigating To Dynamic Routes",
      "lectureOrder": 273,
      "videoOrder": 261,
      "sourceHash": "9a630cbcbf092a0d63e1c979a8a797f09a927670b7a04714064985d11f79d911",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.51,
          "end": 4.77,
          "en": "So in order to load the same tasks component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.77,
          "end": 8.4,
          "en": "with different data for different users,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.4,
          "end": 13.14,
          "en": "I want to make sure that the user ID is actually encoded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 13.14,
          "end": 14.59,
          "en": "in the path up here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.66,
          "end": 19.38,
          "en": "so that we, for example, navigate to slash users",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.38,
          "end": 22.173,
          "en": "slash U three slash tasks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 23.25,
          "end": 27,
          "en": "And the goal then would be to load the tasks component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 27,
          "end": 31.71,
          "en": "but in that component, we should then be able to extract",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 31.71,
          "end": 36.27,
          "en": "that user ID to then fetch the tasks for the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 36.27,
          "end": 38.77,
          "en": "for whom the component was loaded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 40.2,
          "end": 44.04,
          "en": "so that we can reuse the route configuration and component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 44.04,
          "end": 48.15,
          "en": "and still work with different data for different routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 48.15,
          "end": 49.833,
          "en": "or for different paths.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 50.79,
          "end": 53.73,
          "en": "And that's actually a very common requirement,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 53.73,
          "end": 55.86,
          "en": "which is why Angular's router,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 55.86,
          "end": 60.86,
          "en": "like most routers of any framework, allows you to configure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 61.2,
          "end": 63.24,
          "en": "so-called dynamic routes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 63.24,
          "end": 66.51,
          "en": "which are routes where at least parts of the path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 66.51,
          "end": 69.633,
          "en": "are dynamic and not hardcoded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 70.71000000000001,
          "end": 74.76,
          "en": "So here, I'll actually replace my tasks route here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 74.76,
          "end": 77.78999999999999,
          "en": "with a new route where I'll set the path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 77.78999999999999,
          "end": 82.78999999999999,
          "en": "to users slash, let's say, colon user ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 84.48,
          "end": 87.99,
          "en": "And this part here, colon user ID,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 87.99,
          "end": 91.413,
          "en": "would now be a dynamic path segment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 92.61,
          "end": 96.45,
          "en": "Now just to be clear, you don't need users slash here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 96.45,
          "end": 99.57,
          "en": "You could also set up a dynamic path like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 99.57,
          "end": 104.07300000000001,
          "en": "So it may consist of only the dynamic path segment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 105.06,
          "end": 108.84,
          "en": "But here, I actually want to prefix it with users slash",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 108.84,
          "end": 110.97,
          "en": "so that this becomes active",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 110.97,
          "end": 114.39,
          "en": "for your domain slash users slash",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 114.39,
          "end": 116.75999999999999,
          "en": "and then any user ID of your choice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 116.75999999999999,
          "end": 121.59,
          "en": "So for example, one or five or 10 or ABC",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 121.59,
          "end": 126.59,
          "en": "or U one or whatever value can be used as a user ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 128.4,
          "end": 132.87,
          "en": "So that's the idea behind this kind of path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 132.87,
          "end": 135.63,
          "en": "That sets up a dynamic route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 135.63,
          "end": 139.56,
          "en": "because we have a dynamic path segment in here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 139.56,
          "end": 143.25,
          "en": "and you could have multiple dynamic path segments",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 143.25,
          "end": 145.41,
          "en": "in a single route if you needed them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 145.41,
          "end": 149.52,
          "en": "But here, I'm fine with just the user ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 149.52,
          "end": 152.4,
          "en": "It's also worth noting that this identifier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 152.4,
          "end": 155.61,
          "en": "after the colon is entirely up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 155.61,
          "end": 160.61,
          "en": "You could also use UID here, or just U or just ID",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 160.86,
          "end": 162.54,
          "en": "or whatever you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 162.54,
          "end": 167.16,
          "en": "But we'll later need this placeholder here, this identifier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 167.16,
          "end": 171.69,
          "en": "to extract the actual user ID from the URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 171.69,
          "end": 174.51,
          "en": "so that we can then load the right data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 174.51,
          "end": 176.163,
          "en": "for the selected user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 177.03,
          "end": 179.16,
          "en": "But it is up to you how you name this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 179.16,
          "end": 181.74,
          "en": "This colon on the other hand, is required",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 181.74,
          "end": 184.11,
          "en": "because that is what tells Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 184.11,
          "end": 186.453,
          "en": "that you have a dynamic segment here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 187.62,
          "end": 189.03,
          "en": "Well, and besides that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 189.03,
          "end": 191.97,
          "en": "this route is then still set up as before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 191.97,
          "end": 195.24,
          "en": "you define the component that should be loaded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 195.24,
          "end": 197.28300000000002,
          "en": "for this user ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 198.32999999999998,
          "end": 201.45,
          "en": "And here, I'll actually load a different component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 201.45,
          "end": 204.42000000000002,
          "en": "a user tasks component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 204.42000000000002,
          "end": 207.273,
          "en": "which I also prepared in advance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 208.14,
          "end": 211.07999999999998,
          "en": "We'll load the tasks component again later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 211.07999999999998,
          "end": 215.133,
          "en": "But for the moment, I'll load the user tasks component here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 216.48,
          "end": 220.95,
          "en": "And this is a component you find in the user's folder there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 220.95,
          "end": 222.123,
          "en": "user tasks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 223.05,
          "end": 226.68,
          "en": "And the goal here is to have some shared header",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 226.68,
          "end": 227.94,
          "en": "for all users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 227.94,
          "end": 229.07999999999998,
          "en": "And then below that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 229.07999999999998,
          "end": 234.07999999999998,
          "en": "I later want to output the different user specific tasks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 234.3,
          "end": 237.24,
          "en": "For the moment, it'll be, of course, the same content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 237.24,
          "end": 239.16,
          "en": "that will be displayed for all users,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 239.16,
          "end": 242.13,
          "en": "but will soon customize this content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 242.13,
          "end": 245.58,
          "en": "Nonetheless, we now get a dynamic route here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 245.58,
          "end": 250.02,
          "en": "and we therefore now have to go to our user component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 250.02,
          "end": 251.73,
          "en": "where we have this link,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 251.73,
          "end": 254.46,
          "en": "and we have to make sure that we navigate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 254.46,
          "end": 257.25,
          "en": "to this dynamic route here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 257.25,
          "end": 261.36,
          "en": "because going to slash tasks won't do anything anymore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 261.36,
          "end": 264.39300000000003,
          "en": "because we have no slash tasks route anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 265.77,
          "end": 268.83,
          "en": "So instead, we want to go to slash users,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 268.83,
          "end": 272.13,
          "en": "and then the ID of the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 272.13,
          "end": 276.21,
          "en": "for whom this user component is being rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 276.21,
          "end": 280.98,
          "en": "Because keep in mind that we get the user as an input here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 280.98,
          "end": 282.51,
          "en": "here as a Signal input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 282.51,
          "end": 284.85,
          "en": "but of course, it would be the same if you would get it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 284.85,
          "end": 286.563,
          "en": "with the input decorator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 288.27,
          "end": 292.11,
          "en": "So we want to construct this router link dynamically here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 292.11,
          "end": 295.743,
          "en": "and therefore we need, you guessed it, property binding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 297.09000000000003,
          "end": 299.4,
          "en": "And you can now set this in different ways.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 299.4,
          "end": 303.45,
          "en": "You could, for example, construct a string dynamically here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 303.45,
          "end": 305.52,
          "en": "and go to slash users",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 305.52,
          "end": 309.543,
          "en": "and then concatenate user ID like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 310.98,
          "end": 314.64,
          "en": "That would overall set the router link to a string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 314.64,
          "end": 318.03,
          "en": "that contains slash users slash",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 318.03,
          "end": 319.773,
          "en": "and then the ID of the user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 320.88,
          "end": 323.133,
          "en": "This slash here is important by the way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 324.57,
          "end": 327.75,
          "en": "But alternatively, Angular also allows you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 327.75,
          "end": 331.35,
          "en": "to construct this router link path in a different way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 331.35,
          "end": 333.87,
          "en": "if you need to set it dynamically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 333.87,
          "end": 337.62,
          "en": "because Angular also allows you to pass an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 337.62,
          "end": 340.40999999999997,
          "en": "as a value for the router link directive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 340.40999999999997,
          "end": 342.48,
          "en": "instead of passing a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 342.48,
          "end": 344.79,
          "en": "And that array then simply allows you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 344.79,
          "end": 348.18,
          "en": "to define the different path segments",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 348.18,
          "end": 350.58299999999997,
          "en": "as different array elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 351.63,
          "end": 355.47,
          "en": "So for example, the first segment could be slash users,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 355.47,
          "end": 357.87,
          "en": "so this hardcoded string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 357.87,
          "end": 362.64,
          "en": "But the second segment then could be user ID",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 362.64,
          "end": 365.49,
          "en": "and the slash after slash users",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 365.49,
          "end": 368.52,
          "en": "would be inserted automatically by Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 368.52,
          "end": 372.42,
          "en": "because it will basically concatenate these route segments",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 372.42,
          "end": 374.613,
          "en": "by inserting slashes between them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 376.77,
          "end": 378.42,
          "en": "So that's a different notation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 378.42,
          "end": 380.313,
          "en": "which you'll also see quite a bit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 381.27,
          "end": 384.57,
          "en": "And with that, if we saved that, you will see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 384.57,
          "end": 387.69,
          "en": "that if you now hover over these different users,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 387.69,
          "end": 391.29,
          "en": "a different path shows up in the bottom left corner.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 391.29,
          "end": 395.94,
          "en": "And if you click on a user, this path here is loaded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 395.94,
          "end": 397.86,
          "en": "or is added to the URL,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 397.86,
          "end": 401.37,
          "en": "and it's now only this user that's marked as active",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 401.37,
          "end": 405.183,
          "en": "because every user item here now has a different path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 406.47,
          "end": 410.28,
          "en": "As you can see, if you watch this URL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 410.28,
          "end": 412.65,
          "en": "You see the user ID changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 412.65,
          "end": 416.043,
          "en": "as I switch between different users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 417.99,
          "end": 421.26,
          "en": "And that's the offer, how you can set up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 421.26,
          "end": 423.753,
          "en": "and use dynamic routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 424.59,
          "end": 428.43,
          "en": "As a next step, it would of course be great if we could go",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 428.43,
          "end": 432.15,
          "en": "to the user tasks component, which is the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 432.15,
          "end": 434.64,
          "en": "that is loaded with this dynamic route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 434.64,
          "end": 437.91,
          "en": "And in there, I now wanna output a different username",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 437.91,
          "end": 439.29,
          "en": "for every user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 439.29,
          "end": 441.303,
          "en": "So that's what we'll do next.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
